# Frontend Browser Compatibility Rules

## Related Rules
- @frontend/core/performance.mdc for performance optimization
- @frontend/core/accessibility.mdc for cross-browser accessibility
- @frontend/core/error-handling.mdc for graceful degradation

## Core Principles
1. **Browser Support**
   - Define supported browsers
   - Set minimum versions
   - Handle unsupported browsers
   - Test across browsers
   - Monitor usage statistics

2. **Implementation Guidelines**
   - Use feature detection
   - Implement polyfills
   - Handle vendor prefixes
   - Support progressive enhancement
   - Implement graceful degradation

## Browser Support Matrix
- Chrome (last 2 versions)
- Firefox (last 2 versions)
- Safari (last 2 versions)
- Edge (last 2 versions)
- iOS Safari (last 2 versions)
- Android Chrome (last 2 versions)

## Implementation Patterns

### Feature Detection
```javascript
// Example: Feature detection
if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
  // Use IntersectionObserver
} else {
  // Fallback implementation
}
```

### Polyfills
```javascript
// Example: Polyfill usage
import 'core-js/stable';
import 'regenerator-runtime/runtime';
```

### Vendor Prefixes
```css
/* Example: Vendor prefixes */
.selector {
  -webkit-transition: all 0.3s ease;
  -moz-transition: all 0.3s ease;
  -ms-transition: all 0.3s ease;
  -o-transition: all 0.3s ease;
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}
```

## CSS Compatibility
- Use autoprefixer
- Handle flexbox fallbacks
- Support grid layouts
- Handle custom properties
- Support media queries

## JavaScript Compatibility
- Use Babel for transpilation
- Handle ES6+ features
- Support async/await
- Handle modules
- Support promises

## HTML Compatibility
- Use semantic HTML
- Support custom elements
- Handle form validation
- Support web components
- Handle shadow DOM

## Performance Considerations
- Optimize polyfills
- Minimize bundle size
- Handle loading strategies
- Support code splitting
- Implement lazy loading

## Testing Requirements
- Test across browsers
- Verify feature support
- Check polyfills
- Test fallbacks
- Verify performance
- Check accessibility

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Not defining browser support
- Not using feature detection
- Not implementing polyfills
- Not handling vendor prefixes
- Not testing across browsers
- Not monitoring usage
- Not optimizing performance
- Not supporting fallbacks
- Not checking accessibility
- Not documenting requirements

